Did you take out the seconds or minutes timer and flip it over?

Did you make a copy of the robot that is trained to subtract when
the number gets too big?

Did you point to the first 0 and type 23?

Did you point to the second 0 and type -24?

Did you flip the timer over and put it back in the box?

Did you put the robot copy on the back of the hours timers?

Did you put the box with the -24 on the back of the hours timer?

Did you flip the timer back over and put it back in the box?

So this is what I'd do.  I'd take the seconds timer out and flip it over.  I'd
take out the robot trained to subtract when the number gets too
big.  Then I'd copy that robot.  I'd put the robot I took from the seconds
timer back.  I'd pick up the 0 in the third hole and type 23 and put it back.
Then I'd pick other 0 and type -24 and put the -24 back.
Then I'd put the robot copy on the back of the hours
timer and give him the box. Then I'd flip the hours timer over and put it back
in the box and bring it back.


